From bf43b962b78e89c541a84a8ead8f61c6989222fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 17:15:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 55/59] net: add the minimal DNS responder for the rescue page
 (task-97)

Port the bl-mt798x-dhcpd DNS server (release 2026-10-08, GPL-2.0,
Copyright Yuzhii0718) so the rescue page can be reached by name
instead of only by address.

The wire helpers (encoded-name parsing, case-insensitive matching and
the A-record reply layout) live in include/net/mtk_dnsd.h so a host
fixture can test them without the network stack.  The handler answers
A queries for one domain from the dnsd_domain environment variable
(default failsafe.lan) with the active net_ip, returns NXDOMAIN for
other names and NOERROR/NODATA for non-A queries, and chains any
unrelated UDP traffic to the previous handler.

e2631rescue starts the server after DHCP; a DNS failure only warns,
because the rescue must not depend on the convenience name.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
